   ATTRIBUTION.md source-header lines. The signed skeleton was pushed first.
2. Protocol — src/protocol/mod.rs:713 exports the schemars schema;
   protocol.schema.json is checked against it. tests/protocol_golden.rs:295
   verifies exact JSONL round trips for five fixtures under
   tests/fixtures/protocol. They cover all item kinds, text/reasoning, parallel
   reads, FileChange, Terminal, Plan, Approval, interruption, recovery, Lagged
   and Reset. src/protocol/laws.rs:23 enforces lifecycle/pairing/durable ordering.
   tests/protocol_laws.rs:15 supplies broken transcripts. The protocol/fixtures
   were pushed early at e438e2e for the GUI consumer.
3. Core — src/engine/mod.rs:82 owns the 64-entry work lane, separate 256-entry
   control FIFO, 1024-op deduplication cache, turn/steer queues and approvals.
   Bounded work batches preserve control and completion progress; fallback
   steers retain admission order. src/engine/turn_loop.rs:35 is the shared Yarn
   topology and :125 joins children and synthesizes unfinished results before
   the ending. task_group.rs:10 owns cancellation and JoinSet tasks.
   process.rs:43 kills its own process group, drains pipes and reaps the leader.
   provider/parser.rs:16 strictly assembles indexed calls; provider/mod.rs:114
   implements pre-output retry, Retry-After and cancellable HTTP.
   tools.rs:174 checks permits, concurrency classes and path locks; exact edit
   misses report suggestions, apply_patch stages all edits, and capped output
   spills to redacted content-addressed blobs. policy.rs:76 uses data rules and
   unattended deny. store.rs:172 writes before publish; :223 recovers children
   first, pairs calls and closes turns. gateway/mod.rs:392/:443 admit and replay
   without awaiting a face; replay is lazy. gateway/unix.rs:144 demultiplexes
   correlated replies and envelopes, with a five-second unknown-outcome timeout.
   headless.rs:43 and seat.rs:9 provide JSONL and append-only line projection.
4. Formal — tests/formal/models.rs:47 maps turn lifecycle and synthetic pairing;
   :147 maps A-B-A cancellation; :216 maps control/steer progress; :258 maps
   approval; :324 maps subscriber replay; :450 reuses DirtyWake. The corpus
   includes separate omission, leader-only kill, lag-repair and healthy-peer
   controls. tests/reactor_projection.rs:21 compares all 15 nonempty readiness
