## Scope, limits and worktree state

Deliberately outside this assignment: GUI/window/widgets and upstream workspace
membership; MCP client (optional); ACP adapter. The feature declarations reserve
those integration points. R15 embedded toolkit deduplication was not run in the
other repository. No merge, release or installation was performed.

Finite models abstract contracts. Real HTTP/UTF-8, filesystem durability, kernel
scheduling, wall-clock limits, scrubbing and terminal bytes remain covered by
implementation witnesses. Pixel/rendering claims belong to the GUI assignment.
The API is session-bound: SessionActor::open loads/recoveries a session before
its InProc handle is exposed. There is no multi-session catalogue/daemon that
lazily loads arbitrary session IDs on subscribe. Seat projection currently
prints authoritative completed text; incremental text is available as gateway
snapshots, not printed incrementally by the line renderer. These gateway/seat
ICD details remain gaps, not claimed verification. Compact saves a replay blob;
it does not yet reduce the model context. Fork metadata is retained without
materializing parent history. Idle SetProfile may await key/profile resolution;
control send still admits immediately, but idle profile-load/close latency has
not been proven. These are explicit implementation limits for Oracle review.

U1-U7 interim behavior: credited local exporter/metadata writer (U1); copied
helpers with explicit const variable counts (U2); standalone inventory and hash
inputs, without embedded sub-inventory integration (U3); local mappings instead
of importing private upstream models (U4); renamed projection plus separate
weak-fair semantic model (U5); exported metadata name tables (U6); local scoped
JoinSet/cancellation group and mpsc completion lane marked for replacement by
upstream (U7).

All source and this report are signed and pushed on e1-core. Generated formal
archives remain local untracked run artifacts; the source tree is clean.
The Oracle must inspect the tree/diff and re-run the gates before acceptance.
